! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1262 ("TEST EX AND EXIC"), TEST 3B --
! "-TEST 3B, SUBJ INSTR OF EXITC LESS / -THAN 32.", octal
! 024151.40-024162.00, plus routine 1262's exit and continuity
! bridge, 024162.40-024171.00.  32 half-words, ALL ON PDF p.108.
!
! WHERE THIS FILE CUTS, and why the cut is at 024171.00.  The task
! asked for TEST 3B (024151.40-024162.00, 18 half-words) plus the
! exit/continuity rows that follow "if they are contiguous and
! self-contained".  They are both.  024162.40 "B,$+1.0" begins the
! standard routine-exit sequence this deck uses everywhere (the same
! five rows stand at 024357.40-024361.40 on PDF p.110, ending routine
! 1681), and it runs without a gap through the continuity bridge to
! the continuity register itself, "1C262 XW,0,0,0 -CONTINUITY REG" at
! 024171.00.  That XW is the last printed row on p.108; p.109 opens a
! new block with "CNOP / -CONSTANTS FOR 1262." at 024172.00.  So the
! cut is where the page ends AND where the routine ends, and the 14
! tail rows reference nothing defined after them.
!
! CITED BY PDF PAGE, and that is not a slip.  jb_ax5b's LISTING pages
! carry no printed page numbers at all -- the "12 11 10 9" down the
! left margin is fanfold carriage-tape line numbering, and the only
! printed numbers are in the front write-up, which is scanned 2-up.
! Every verify_ax5b_*.py here already says "PDF p.NN" for that reason.
!
! WHAT TEST 3B CHECKS.  Reference Manual printed p.50 (PDF p.53), read
! at 600 dpi for this file: "Subject instructions of EXECUTE INDIRECT
! AND COUNT may occupy any available locations with addresses 32.00 and
! greater."  It is the SECOND sentence of one paragraph whose first is
! the rule TEST 3A tests ("...cannot occupy locations addressed between
! 0 and 15."), and the page sets a trap for a skimming eye: the right
! column of PDF p.53 OPENS with "15.  Subject instructions of ...",
! where that "15." is the TAIL of the left column's sentence and not a
! list number.  TEST 3A,
! immediately above, put the PSEUDO-IC below 15; TEST 3B leaves the
! pseudo-IC legal (162PSI, 024323.00) and puts the SUBJECT INSTRUCTION
! below 32 instead.  "LVI,$X1,$X0 / SVA,$X1,162PSI" is the whole idea:
! $X0 is index register 0, WORD 16, so its half-word address is 32 --
! the LVI takes that address as a value and the SVA plants it in
! 162PSI's address field, aiming the pseudo-IC at word 16.  Then
! "LX,$X0,162EXI" loads the subject instruction itself into $X0, and
! "EXIC,162PSI" tries to execute it from there.  Its three error
! messages ARE the contract, and all three are printed on p.108,
! read at 600 dpi:
!
!   (a) "-NO INTERRUPT WHEN SUBJ INST OF / -EXIC LESS THAN 32."
!       at 024156.40-024157.00, reached by FALLING THROUGH the EXIC,
!       so the error is that no interruption occurred.
!   (b) "-AD NOT SET WHEN SUBJ INST OF / -EXIC LESS THAN 32."
!       at 024160.00-024160.40, reached from 162104, the handler this
!       test plants in the interrupt entry, when "BADZ,$+1.32" finds
!       AD off.
!   (c) "-SUBJ INST OF EXIC NOT NOPED / -WHEN IT IS LESS THAN 32."
!       at 024161.40-024162.00.  "Z,$X1" zeroes index register 1
!       before the EXIC and the subject at 162EXI is
!       "LVI,$X1,%8@777777.40" (024332.00, PDF p.110, read here), so
!       "LX,$X1,$X1 / BZXVZ,SERS" -- report the error unless the index
!       VALUE is zero -- is literally "the subject never ran".
!
! THE DECK'S OWN TYPO, recorded not corrected.  The heading comment at
! 024151.40 spells the mnemonic "EXITC": five letters, where every one
! of the six later comment lines on this page writes "EXIC".  Settled
! by measurement rather than by eye, because a ruling line runs along
! the cap height of that row and hides the top bar of every letter.
! The comment column is monospaced; fitting the pitch on the row
! "-NO INTERRUPT WHEN SUBJ INST OF" (31 cells) against the four "N"
! glyphs of that row gives 60.1 px per cell at 600 dpi with cell 0 at
! x=2403.  The final "S" of the heading's "LESS" starts at x=4394 =
! cell 33, so the heading is 34 characters -- one more than
! "-TEST 3B, SUBJ INSTR OF EXIC LESS" (33).  There are visibly TWO
! vertical strokes between the X and the C where "-EXIC LESS THAN 32."
! two rows down has one.  Five letters is established; I vs T in the
! fourth is NOT separable under the rule, and "EXITC" is the recorded
! reading.  It joins TEST 3A's "PSEDUO" as a deck typo.
!
! ONE ROW IS NOT EXPLAINED BY THESE PAGES, and TEST 3A's forward
! reference to it is CONFIRMED here first-hand.  At 024155.40, between
! "Z,$X1" and "EXIC,162PSI", stands "%8@DD%BU,32,8@,3740
! -ILLEGAL OP." printing 00000003740 -- byte for byte the same word
! TEST 3A carries at 024144.40, and the same word routine 1260's 160K7
! prints at 023050.00 under "-ILLEGAL OP, NO. 31."
! (programs/ax5b_160k_constants.strap).  ax5b_162_test3a.strap said
! TEST 3B "repeats the identical Z,$X1 / DD / EXIC triple at
! 024155.00/024155.40/024156.00"; it does, exactly there, and this
! transcription read it off the page rather than taking 3A's word for
! it.  What that upgrades is only the status of the observation: an
! operation-code-invalid word standing in the straight-line
! instruction path, one half-word before the EXIC, is now known to be
! SYSTEMATIC in this routine rather than a one-off slip.  Nothing on
! pp.107-110 says why.
!
! TEST 1CC EXPLAINS WHAT THE WORD IS, AND DOES NOT EXPLAIN WHAT IT IS
! DOING HERE.  Both halves matter.  1CC (pp.93-94) uses the identical
! word twice, in OPPOSITE polarities, as a PROBE FOR THE ENABLE STATE:
! an operation-code-invalid word actuates OP, indicator 15, and mask
! bits 0-19 are permanently one (StretchTypes.bsv:271 gives ind_OP =
! 15), so executing one interrupts IF AND ONLY IF the interruption
! system is enabled.  1CC's error text proves the reading in both
! directions -- "-SYSTEM ENABLED AFTER EX OF / -A BE INSTRUCTION."
! where it must NOT interrupt, and "-SYSTEM DISABLED AFTER EX OF / -A
! BD INSTRUCTION." where it must.  That is a settled mechanism from a
! deck oracle, not a guess.
!
! BUT THE MECHANISM DOES NOT FIT THIS BLOCK, and saying how it fails is
! the honest report.  Read straight through, 024155.40's DD stands
! between "Z,$X1" and the EXIC.  The OK path out of the EXIC is an
! INTERRUPT -- that is what makes 024156.40's fall-through error
! "-NO INTERRUPT WHEN SUBJ INST OF / -EXIC LESS THAN 32." and what the
! SVA at 024154.40 plants L162104 for.  So the system must be ENABLED
! when 024156.00 runs.  If it is also enabled one half-word earlier,
! the DD interrupts FIRST, vectors to the same L162104 (024157.40),
! and arrives with OP set and AD clear -- so the BADZ there would fall
! through to "-AD NOT SET WHEN SUBJ INST OF / -EXIC LESS THAN 32.",
! and the EXIC under test would never execute at all.  The block
! cannot pass under that reading, and the deck presumably passed.
!
! SO SOMETHING IN THE READING IS WRONG, AND THIS FILE DOES NOT KNOW
! WHICH.  The candidates, none checked against a primary source:
! 024152.40-024153.00's call into 1260's clear-indicators subroutine
! may return DISABLED and something between it and the EXIC may
! re-enable; 162ITE's landing half may be a BD, so a first interrupt
! disables and the DD is the deliberate arming step rather than a
! probe; or the DD is simply not executed, which would need a rule
! about data words in the instruction stream that neither page states.
! Settling it needs the pages this file did not transcribe -- 160S1 at
! 022741.00 (pp.83-85) and 162ITE at 024320.00 (p.109) -- not more
! inference from the rows above.  Recorded as an OPEN QUESTION with a
! named next step, which is a better position than the "unexplained
! row" 3A left and a better one than pretending 1CC closed it.
!
! Stated rather than rationalised, in the manner
! of ax5b_16082_op_ad.strap's "NOT TRACED" block; the ENCODING of the
! row is settled either way, and that is what this file checks.
!
! NO MNEMONIC IS A FIRST HERE, and that was checked by grep, not
! assumed: LVI, SVA, SIC, B, LX, Z, EXIC, BD, BADZ, BZXVZ and SX are
! all in verify_ax5b_162_test3a_listing.py's own rows; DD is in
! verify_ax5b_1258_test2_listing.py; KVI, V+, BZXE, CNOP and XW are in
! five, thirteen, eight, twelve and thirty-three verify files each.
! What TEST 3B adds:
!   - a THIRD independent listing witness for EXIC (TEST 2B's
!     "EXIC,162PSI", TEST 3A's "EXIC,$R", and this one), and the
!     only one of the three whose failure mode is the SUBJECT's
!     address rather than the pseudo-IC's;
!   - the first row anywhere in this repo with an INDEX REGISTER in an
!     immediate-index VALUE field -- "LVI,$X1,$X0" at 024151.40, which
!     pins $X0 at word 16 (address 20.03 01, addr19 = 32).  Every
!     other $X0 in a verify file is a J field;
!   - the first self-relative row whose COMPUTED target has bit 18 set
!     -- "B,$+1.0" at 024162.40 -> 024163.40.  TEST 3A's only
!     self-relative row, "$+1.32", lands on a .00;
!   - B and BD side by side under the same operand: 024160.40 is
!     "B,SERS" where TEST 3A's matching rule-(b) row was "BD,SERS".
!     One block now discriminates the two unconditional-branch codes.
!
! ENCODING ONLY, and it could not be otherwise: a run needs the
! 64-word interrupt table, SSIP's SEN/SERS reporting, 160S1's body,
! and an EXIC the model actually EXECUTES.  EXIC is in MISC_CODES, so
! the ASSEMBLER encodes it; that is the whole distinction.
!
! Transcription standard: bit-exact against the printed machine code,
! verify_ax5b_162_test3b_listing.py.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: two, the same two TEST 3A made.  Numeric labels take
! an "L" prefix (L162100, L162104, L168), and "1C262" becomes LIC262
! -- the same spelling ax5b_160_test8b.strap uses for "1C260" and
! ax5b_1258_test2.strap for "1C258".  The leading glyph is a bare
! vertical stroke and no measurement separates it from a letter I: in
! this print chain the digit 1 has no flag, so "162100" and
! "INTERRUPT" begin with the same 12-14 px stem at 600 dpi.  The
! reading rests on the naming scheme -- 1C258, 1C260, 1C262 and, on
! the separately read PDF p.110, "Z,1C268" at 024335.00 inside routine
! 1268 -- one continuity register per routine, named for its routine
! number.  (The neighbouring O-vs-0 question DOES yield to
! measurement, and goes the other way: at 024163.40 the glyph after
! SEN is 44 px, matching the digit 0 of "BD,162100" on this page,
! 44-45 px, against 50-51 px for the letter O of "-NO INTERRUPT WHEN
! SUBJ INST OF".  So SEN0, with the digit -- which is how
! ax5b_160_test8b.strap spells it and not how
! verify_ax5b_1258_test2_listing.py's "SENO" does.)  And the DD's
! datum, printed
! "%8@DD%BU,32,8@,3740", is written "(8)3740": assembling it as a bare
! "3740" produces 00000007234, because this assembler's default radix
! is DECIMAL and the listing's is octal.  The "(8)" is load-bearing.
!
! EXTERNALS, SYN'd at the addresses this listing prints.  THESE ARE
! INPUTS TO THE CHECK, NOT WITNESSES -- the same caveat
! verify_ax5b_16082_16083_listing.py makes about L16088.  A SYN row
! MAKES the address field come out right, so the rows naming one prove
! only that every OTHER field lands where the listing puts it.
! Corroboration exists for most of them and none of it converts an
! input into a witness: 162ITE (024320.00), 162PSI (024323.00),
! 162EXI (024332.00) and L168 (024333.00) were each read at 600 dpi
! out of the LABEL COLUMN of PDF pp.109-110 for this transcription;
! SEN0 (001311.00) and SSW (001301.00) are corroborated by the
! identical exit sequence printed at 024360.40-024361.00 on p.110, and
! also appear in ax5b_160_test8b.strap; BIT8 = 024532.00 is the bit
! table's base 024522 plus 8, matching 8b's LBIT11 = 024535.00;
! L162100 = 024136.00 is TEST 3A's entry label; SEN, SERS, 160SX1 and
! 160S1 rest on other verify files in this repo.
!
! THE BLOCK'S GENUINE ADDRESS WITNESSES are THREE, and TEST 3B is a
! better-anchored block than TEST 3A for a reason worth naming: its
! FIRST ROW CARRIES NO LABEL.  TEST 3A had to disclaim L162100,
! because the SLC set the counter and L162100 was the very next label,
! so checking it checked the SLC against the number handed to the SLC.
! Here the first label, L162104, is TWELVE half-words downstream of
! the SLC -- it lands right only if all twelve preceding rows are
! sized right.  The three:
!   - L162104 at 024157.40, reached by the LVI at 024154.00;
!   - LIC262 at 024171.00, thirty-one half-words downstream, and
!     actually tested by the two rows that name it (024165.00 and
!     024166.00);
!   - the self-relative rows 024157.40 "$+1.32", 024162.40 "$+1.0" and
!     024164.40 "$+.32", which depend on no symbol at all.
! LIC262's own CONTENT witnesses nothing -- XW,0,0,0 assembles to all
! zeros under any field layout -- so only its ADDRESS counts.

L160SX1 SYN, (8)23041.0            ! 1260's SIC return link (also p.41)
L160S1  SYN, (8)22741.0            ! 1260's "CLR INDS 0-19" subroutine
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0             ! the SIC error-entry link
SEN0    SYN, (8)1311.0             ! the no-error SIC entry (p.110 too)
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0             ! the error-report routine
SSW     SYN, (8)1301.0             ! SSIP's sense-switch entry (p.110)
BIT8    SYN, (8)24532.0            ! bit table 024522 + 8
L162100 SYN, (8)24136.0            ! TEST 3A's entry, PDF p.107
L162ITE SYN, (8)24320.0            ! "-ALL INTERRUPTS ENTER HERE", p.109
L162PSI SYN, (8)24323.0            ! the pseudo-IC word, PDF p.109
L162EXI SYN, (8)24332.0            ! the IMMED IX subject, PDF p.110
L168    SYN, (8)24333.0            ! routine 168's entry, PDF p.110
        SLC, (8)24151.40
!
! ---- aim the pseudo-IC at $X0, which is word 16, so below 32 -------
        LVI, $X1, $X0              ! -TEST 3B, SUBJ INSTR OF EXITC LESS
        SVA, $X1, L162PSI          ! -THAN 32.
        SIC, L160SX1               ! -CLR INDS 0-19
        B,   L160S1
        LX,  $X0, L162EXI          ! the subject instruction, into word 16
        LVI, $X1, L162104
        SVA, $X1, L162ITE          ! plant the handler in the entry
        Z,   $X1                   ! so a subject that ran shows up
        DD(BU,32,8), (8)3740       ! -ILLEGAL OP.  (see header)
        EXIC, L162PSI
        SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INTERRUPT WHEN SUBJ INST OF
        BD,  SERS                  ! -EXIC LESS THAN 32.
!
! ---- 162104: where the interruption lands; rules (b) and (c) -------
L162104 BADZ, $+1.32               ! AD on -> skip the error, clearing it
        SIC, SEN                   ! -AD NOT SET WHEN SUBJ INST OF
        B,   SERS                  ! -EXIC LESS THAN 32.   (B, not BD)
        LX,  $X1, $X1
        SIC, SEN                   ! -SUBJ INST OF EXIC NOT NOPED
        BZXVZ, SERS                ! -WHEN IT IS LESS THAN 32.
!
! ---- routine 1262's exit, then the continuity bridge ---------------
        B,   $+1.0                 ! computed target 024163.40, bit 18 = 1
        BD,  L162100               ! the restart link: TEST 3A's entry
        SIC, SEN0+.32
        B,   SSW                   ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
        LX,  $X13, LIC262          ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        V+,  $X13, BIT8            ! routine 1262 done = bit 8
        SX,  $X13, LIC262
        KVI, $X13, (8)777000.0     ! compare the whole continuity mask
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -CONTINUITY ERROR.
        BD,  L168                  ! on to routine 168, PDF p.110
        CNOP
LIC262  XW, 0, 0, 0                ! -CONTINUITY REG
        END, (8)24151.40
